course: dictionary
lesson: 5013
title: Infinity: the word that never ends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Infinity means something that has no end and goes on for ever. Context clues can show you this: «The Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama makes Infinity Mirror Rooms where mirrors and lights make the space look endless.» Endless is the clue. Something endless has no end, so infinity must mean the same kind of thing.
explain: In maths, infinity is not a normal number. There is no biggest number, because you can always add 1, so counting numbers go on to infinity. Mathematicians show infinity with the symbol ∞.
explain: Infinity can also mean an extremely large or endless amount. To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Here, «endless» fits, so your meaning works.
fact: Infinity means having no end, going on for ever and bigger than any number.
fact: The symbol for infinity is ∞.
fact: Art that fills a room, like Kusama's Infinity Mirror Rooms, is called an installation.
fact: «To infinity and beyond» is a famous line from the film Toy Story.
fact: Infinity is not a normal number, so you cannot do sums like infinity minus infinity.
exercise: «The mirrors made the room look endless.» What does endless mean here? | *Going on for ever, with no end | Very small | Bright and yellow | Full of people
exercise: Which symbol shows infinity? | % | *∞ | # | 5
exercise: In maths, what is true about counting numbers? | *They go on to infinity, so there is no biggest one | There is a biggest number, and it is 100 | They stop at ten | They are all the same
test: Which sentence uses infinity to mean an extremely large or endless amount? | *The night sky seemed to hold an infinity of stars. | The soup was warm. | My shoes are under the bed. | The bus stopped at the corner.
test: Why can't you do infinity minus infinity as a normal sum? | Because infinity is a colour. | *Infinity is not a normal number, so normal sums do not work with it. | Because the answer is always ten. | Because subtraction is only for small numbers.
exam: What is the best meaning of infinity? | *Something with no end that goes on for ever | A kind of animal | A word for a broken clock | A very small number
